      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: original transparent production sprite atlas for the hand-painted Ash & Aether RPG, landscape 4 columns by 2 rows, EIGHT isolated architecture WINDOW BAYS. Each is a modest single wall bay with one clear window opening, supporting plaster/stone/timber, a shallow eave or lintel and integrated sill. These are NOT entire houses and NEVER doors. They will be fitted into actual 64-pixel-tall building walls at 38–54 pixels high, so use bold coherent material masses and restrained details that survive small size. STYLE reference: existing A&A gouache construction details, warm clay plaster, weathered deep-brown timber, cool limestone, muted blue/verdigris, gentle upper-left daylight. Painterly watercolor/gouache edges and physical weathering, rounded irregular silhouette, low specularity, no photorealism. Camera: orthographic front-facing elevation with a slight elevated view showing the tops of sills/eaves; wall face square to camera, no left/right yaw or trapezoid perspective. Top row left to right: 1 HOME: bowed dark timber frame surrounding patched warm limewash, a small amber double casement, a thin terracotta tiled eave and a compact rose/thyme sill box; 2 CLINIC: cool chalk-white and pale sage plaster, a broad airy pale blue glazed casement, herb drying slats and a simple pale stone sill, tiny sage sprigs, clinical cleanliness without modern signs; 3 INSTRUMENTWORKS: honey-brown timber and ochre clay infill, an arched blue glass fanlight over a small window, carved abstract sound-wave/lyre-like timber ribs, a brass resonator disk integrated in the lintel, handmade music workshop identity; 4 INN/KITCHEN: warm weathered brick and limewash bay with a small dark serving window, muted indigo half-shutter, rounded tiled hood, a tiny bread crock on the broad sill, hospitable but not a shop counter extending into ground. Bottom row left to right: 5 GUILD/ARCHIVE: cool limestone surround with two narrow indigo leaded panes within one bay, horizontal carved lintel, restrained brass corner fittings, two abstract sealed tablets integrated below the sill with NO legible writing; 6 CARPENTER/WORKSHOP: stout repaired timber-framed limewash bay, small open slatted shutter window, visible pegged joinery and a thin closed wall tool rack with one plane and wood pegs, compact sawtooth eave; 7 CHAPEL: pale weathered limestone single arched window bay with muted dusty-blue and honey glass, a small curved stone moulding and worn abstract three-lobed relief above, contemplative without symbols or signage; 8 CISTERN: blue-green weathered glazed brick bay with a small round barred inspection window, a restrained copper water-level vessel integrated at the side and a damp limestone sill, no running water. All wall bases stop at their sill/plinth, no floor, no ground, no courtyard paving, no steps, no entry holes large enough for people, no figures, no text/labels/numbers/watermark. True transparent alpha background. Every sprite must be fully complete and entirely separated from neighbors by wide transparent gutters at least 10% of each cell; leave a substantial transparent outside margin. Exactly 8 distinct objects in exact 4×2 ordering, no extra items between cells. Every prop fits safely inside its own nominal cell including its shadow and foliage. No checkerboard baked into pixels.",
