      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: original transparent production architecture-craft sprite atlas for the Ash & Aether painted RPG. Create EXACTLY EIGHT complete distinct modular building details in a 4-column by 2-row landscape grid. They will be mounted only to existing roofs, gables, wallposts and courtyard returns, at 18–46 world pixels high. Strong simple silhouettes and large coherent material masses must stay readable at that size. Match weathered hand-painted gouache / watercolor A&A art: warm clay and deep-brown timber, cool blue stone, muted sage, restrained aged copper/brass, gentle upper-left light, restrained integrated contact shadow. Elevated orthographic camera roughly30–35 degrees showing roofs/vent caps, no dramatic perspective; wall-mounted pieces face straight forward without sideways yaw. NO ground plates, whole houses, doors, stairs, paving, people, symbols, lettering, smoke or exterior scenic backgrounds. Top row left to right: 1 DOMESTIC CHIMNEY: compact slightly bowed terracotta-brick chimney stack with a broad pale limestone cap and two short dark clay pots of unequal height, weathered ochre mortar, a little low moss at its base; 2 INSTRUMENTWORKS ROOF VENT: squat dark-timber rooftop sound vent with a curved verdigris copper hood and three visible brass resonator reeds/slats, a small square roof mounting base, finely handmade but structurally bold; 3 CLINIC ROOF VENT: compact pale sage ceramic air ventilator with four large slats, low rounded cream hood, glazed weathering and simple lead flashing at its narrow base, restful clean silhouette; 4 ARCHIVE/GUILD RIDGE VENT: low blue-slate gabled rooftop ventilator with a prominent single round honey-brass grille and dark timber framing, small grey flashing at its base, no flag or arrow. Bottom row left to right: 5 CARPENTER GABLE TRUSS: broad triangular dark-timber gable ornament, open negative spaces between five heavy curved braces, pegged carved joinery, shallow warm ochre fascia edge; a complete wall-mounted triangle approximately twice as wide as tall, NO roof of a whole house; 6 CHAPEL STONE MEDALLION: simple worn rounded limestone carved relief with an abstract triple-lobed recess and three restrained dusty-blue glazed inlays, deeply weathered edges, no cross, no letters, no enclosing wall plate; 7 CISTERN RAIN HOPPER: a vertical aged-copper rain hopper with wide rounded vessel top, short bent downpipe with two clear mounting brackets, muted verdigris, complete closed bottom, NO flowing water; 8 COURTYARD RETURN: narrow squat weathered limestone pilaster section with a rounded cap and irregular sculptural ivy, a single small terracotta herb pot nestled against its base; a wall-attached construction detail, NOT a freestanding gateway, NO doorway, NO pavement. True transparent alpha. Each of8objects must fit entirely inside its own nominal cell including all foliage, braces and contact shade. Wide clear gutters of at least10% cellsize plus transparent outside margins. Do not let caps, thin pipes or ivy touch any neighbor or image edge. No checkerboard pattern in pixels, no cast shadows extending across cells, no glow.",
